}
```

Here's the output.
Note that `employees.Data` stays a braced struct because only its `Members` field was flattened; the other groups' `Data` fields were already flat:

```
employees.Description: "This group lists all the employees."
employees.Data: {
	Members+: 'alice'
	Members+: 'bob'
	Members+: 'charlie'
	Members+: 'dave'
	Members+: 'frank'
}

developers.Description: '''
	This group lists all the developers.
	They have write access to the code repository.
	'''
developers.Data.Members+: 'alice'
developers.Data.Members+: 'charlie'
# Frank is both a developer and sysadmin.
developers.Data.Members+: 'frank'

sysadmins.Description: ''''|This group lists all the employees with production access.''''

sysadmins.Data.Members+: 'bob'
sysadmins.Data.Members+: 'dave'
sysadmins.Data.Members+: 'frank'  # Frank is both a developer and sysadmin.
```

The top-level node returned by `Unmarshal()` is itself a flat struct with an empty name, which is why the file has no enclosing braces.

