## Appendix: pest grammar

Here's a simplified ``https://pest.rs|pest`` grammar for parsing an sdin file:

```
SDINFile = { SOI ~ (NamedValue | WS)* ~ EOI }

NamedValue = ${ Name ~ (" " | "\t")* ~ Value }
Name       = @{ BareToken ~ ":" }
Value      =  { Struct | List | Form | String | BareToken }

Struct    =  { "{" ~ (NamedValue | WS)* ~ "}" }
List      =  { "[" ~ (Value | WS)* ~ "]" }
Form      =  { FormName ~ (NamedValue | Value | WS)* ~ ")" }
FormName  = @{ BareToken ~ "(" }
BareToken =  { BareCharacter+ }

Reserved      = _{ " " | "\t" | "\r" | "\n" | "'" | "\"" | ":" | "#" | "[" | "]" | "{" | "}" | "(" | ")" }
BareCharacter = _{ !Reserved ~ ANY }
Comment       = @{ "#" ~ (!"\n" ~ ANY)* ~ ("\n" | &EOI) }
WS            = _{ " " | "\t" | "\r" | "\n" | Comment }

// Only single quoted strings listed here for brevity.
// String rules are somewhat complicated, unfortunately.
String = @{ "'" ~ (!("'") ~ ANY)* ~ "'" }
```

